---
layout: layouts/page.njk
styles: [region-page]
title: "Gyeonggi-do population-decline areas"
description: "The Gyeonggi-do and Incheon areas that qualify for the F-1-D visa's lower, non-capital income threshold despite sitting inside the capital area."
permalink: "/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-areas/"
---
{# Not paginated like regions/region.njk — Gyeonggi-do is the only capital-tier region, so it's
   the only place a population-decline area can change the eligibility outcome (see ARCHITECTURE.md,
   eligibility gating). Redesign style: same wide .region-page shell + two-column headline as region.njk, with a
   tinted threshold-summary card in place of the rent recap. #}
{% set declineCounties = [] %}
{% set watchCounties = [] %}
{% for c in populationDeclineAreas %}
{% if c.category == "decline" %}{% set pushed = declineCounties.push(c) %}{% else %}{% set pushed = watchCounties.push(c) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% from "partials/photo-credit.njk" import creditText %}
{% set countyPhotos = [] %}
{% for c in populationDeclineAreas %}{% set pushed = countyPhotos.push(countyHeroPhotos[c.countyNameEn]) %}{% endfor %}

{% macro tierCard(c) %}
{% set photo = [countyHeroPhotos[c.countyNameEn] or { file: c.countyNameEn + ": no photo mapped" }] | credited("county card " + c.countyNameEn) | first %}
<li class="tier-card">
  <figure class="tier-card__figure">
    {% if photo %}<img class="tier-card__img" src="/assets/img/hero/gyeonggi-do-population-decline/{{ photo.file }}" alt="{{ photo.titleEn }}" loading="lazy">{% endif %}
    {% if photo.titleEn %}
    <figcaption class="tier-card__spot">
      <span class="tier-card__spot-en">{{ photo.titleEn }}</span>
      {% if photo.titleKo %}<span class="tier-card__spot-ko" lang="ko">{{ photo.titleKo }}</span>{% endif %}
    </figcaption>
    {% endif %}
  </figure>
  <div class="tier-card__body">
    <p class="tier-card__name">{{ c.countyNameEn }} <span class="tier-card__ko" lang="ko">{{ c.countyNameKo }}</span></p>
    <p class="tier-card__metro">{{ c.metroEn }}</p>
  </div>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="content-page region-page county-page">

<nav class="region-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/#map">Regions</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/">Gyeonggi-do</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span class="region-breadcrumb__here">Population-decline areas</span>
</nav>

<header class="region-header region-header--split">
  <div class="region-header__main">
    <span class="region-header__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <h1>Gyeonggi-do population-decline areas</h1>
    <p class="county-page__ko" lang="ko">경기도 인구감소지역</p>
    <p class="region-header__intro">
      Gyeonggi-do is part of Korea's capital area, where the F-1-D income threshold is higher.
      Seven areas are an exception: they qualify for the lower non-capital threshold because they
      are designated as population-decline or watch-list areas.
    </p>
  </div>

  <aside class="region-header__aside">
    <div class="threshold-card">
      <dl class="threshold-card__table">
        <div>
          <dt>These seven areas</dt>
          <dd>₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1"] / 1000000 }}M–{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1.5"] / 1000000 }}M</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Rest of Gyeonggi-do &amp; Incheon</dt>
          <dd>₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1.5"] / 1000000 }}M–{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["2"] / 1000000 }}M</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="threshold-card__note">
        The exact threshold depends on your age and whether you are accompanied by family.
      </p>
      <p class="threshold-card__links">
        <a href="/visa-info/">Visa info →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-plate note-plate--stricter">
      <span class="note-plate__text">This interpretation is <a href="/visa-info/#notes">awaiting ministry confirmation.</a></span>
    </div>
  </aside>
</header>

<section class="region-section">
  <div class="source-note">
    <span class="source-note__head"><span class="source-note__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>Source:</span>
    <div class="region-guides__item">
      <a class="region-guides__link" href="https://www.mois.go.kr/frt/sub/a06/b06/populationDecline/screen.do" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Population-decline area designation ↗</a>
      <span class="region-guides__meta">mois.go.kr · Designation cycle: {{ populationDeclineDesignation.cycle }} · Next expected designation: {{ populationDeclineDesignation.nextExpected | formatDate }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="region-section region-section--tiers">
  <div class="tier-group">
    <p class="tier-label">
      <span class="tier-chip tier-chip--designated">Designated · {{ declineCounties.length }}</span>
      Formally listed as population-decline areas.
    </p>
    <ul class="tier-grid">
      {% for c in declineCounties %}{{ tierCard(c) }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="tier-group">
    <p class="tier-label">
      <span class="tier-chip tier-chip--watch">Watch-list · {{ watchCounties.length }}</span>
      Monitored, not yet designated
    </p>
    <ul class="tier-grid">
      {% for c in watchCounties %}{{ tierCard(c) }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="data-provenance">Source: {{ creditText(countyPhotos | photoCredits) }}.</p>
</section>

</div>
